ur jobs how we do on  our studies as well as even in creative  work for example if we have new creative  ideas and these type of things so you  have probably encountered in the past  this effect that you're really stuck  with an idea and then you go on a  vigorous run or just even a walk and  afterwards you kind of get unstuck or  kind of get a new inspiration or a new  idea so i will here explain some of the  mechanisms that people think are  responsible for this effect so a large  body of research has now shown that  exercise can actually directly change  your brain's function as well as  structure so the structure is just the  amount of gray matter you have and the  gray matter is kind of the spongy  material of your brain and the function  is how you use it or how much blood flow  goes to certain areas of your brain so  my teacher kind of explained it as this  that if the structure are the roads then  the function is the amount of cars that  flow on the road so if you can improve  your roads and you can improve the  amount of cars that can actually  flow on the roads  this would in general improve your brain  so yeah and that's what some people  claim that exercise can do so let's get  into some of the research  so two areas that have been shown to be  directly influenced by doing exercise is  the hippocampal area in the prefrontal  cortex so the hippocampal area is the  area that is directly related for us to  memory so it's kind of our memory center  so the prefrontal cortex has been  related to planning  decision making as well as memory  consolidation so you can imagine if you  can improve your planning that you could  make a better plan for the upcoming exam  season if you could improve your  decision making then perhaps you could  decide not to watch netflix and if you  could improve your memory or memory  retention consolidation then perhaps you  only have to memorize the information  once and already do a better job in that  regard and so we can kind of 